      "title": "Data Science in Iran: Methods, Business Uses and Evidence",
      "description": "Explore data science in Iran’s business context, from operational analysis and BI to forecasting, with clear distinctions between capabilities and verified outcomes."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "scope",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From business records to useful evidence",
        "content": "Data science brings together statistics, programming, and knowledge of the subject being studied. Its purpose is to extract useful insights from data, rather than simply accumulate records or produce elaborate visualizations. IBM’s technical introduction emphasizes this combination of disciplines and connects it to organizational decision-making. A prediction is one possible output; a carefully qualified explanation or a reproducible analysis can be equally valuable. [s1]\n\nFor readers exploring Iranian business, the useful starting point is a question: what decision could better evidence improve? An illustrative distributor might investigate recurring stock shortages; an online service might examine why customers stop returning. These are examples of possible analytical questions, not claims that particular Iranian companies have implemented successful systems. The distinction matters because a plausible application does not establish adoption, commercial scale, or measurable benefit.",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "branches",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "How the branches fit together",
        "content": "This section separates six closely related subjects. Business data analysis investigates a defined operational question. Business intelligence provides recurring reports and shared measures. Data warehousing organizes information for analytical use. Customer behavior analytics examines patterns of interaction and purchasing; demand forecasting estimates future requirements; recommendation systems select potentially relevant items or services. These are editorial distinctions for navigating the subject, rather than mutually exclusive professional categories. IBM’s descriptions likewise show overlap between data science, analysis, and business decision-making. [s1]\n\nA project can cross several branches. For example, an investigation of delivery delays could begin with a one-off analysis and later become a recurring management report. The important boundary is between answering a question once and maintaining a dependable analytical service. The latter requires attention to the whole data lifecycle: collecting information, preparing it, analyzing it, communicating results, and maintaining the surrounding governance and operations. NIST explicitly places these supporting responsibilities within the scope of data science. [s2]",
        "source_ids": ["s1", "s2"]
      },
      {
        "id": "iran-evidence",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "What the Iranian evidence establishes",
        "content": "An Iranian example is Rahkaran, a business software family from System Group, known in Persian as Hamkaran System. Its Persian-language business intelligence brochure describes data integration, analysis, and visualization, including analytical information for finance, sales, logistics, and human resources. This documents a vendor’s account of an enterprise analytics offering. It does not independently demonstrate the accuracy of customer reports, the size of Iran’s analytics market, or productivity improvements attributable to the software. [s3]\n\nPublic economic research supplies a different kind of evidence. The World Bank’s Iran Economic Monitor brings together macroeconomic developments and topics such as financial markets and household welfare. Such publications can help analysts understand external conditions, but they do not replace an organization’s own transaction records. A national trend cannot establish what happened to a particular company, customer group, or province. [s4]",
        "source_ids": ["s3", "s4"]
      },
      {
        "id": "lifecycle",
        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "An analytical project as a feedback loop",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[\"Define the decision and question\"] -->|\"Identify required evidence\"| B[\"Acquire relevant data\"]\n  B -->|\"Inspect and prepare\"| C[\"Document quality and limitations\"]\n  C -->|\"Use appropriate methods\"| D[\"Analyze and evaluate\"]\n  D -->|\"Explain findings and uncertainty\"| E[\"Communicate to decision-makers\"]\n  E -->|\"Review use and new questions\"| A\n```",
        "summary": "This editorial synthesis shows how a question leads to evidence, analysis, communication, and further inquiry. The arrows describe analytical work, not the reporting structure of an Iranian institution.",
        "as_of_date": null,
        "source_ids": ["s2", "s5"]
      },
      {
        "id": "quality",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "Quality is part of the result",
        "content": "A technically sophisticated model cannot repair an undefined business question. Nor does a large dataset automatically represent the population of interest. The National Academies’ account of the data lifecycle starts with whether a question is answerable and which evidence is needed. It also emphasizes the people who will interpret and use the result. For an Iranian application, that means explaining the operational setting rather than presenting a model as a self-contained answer. [s5]\n\nQuality also persists beyond initial cleaning. NIST’s Research Data Framework identifies accuracy, completeness, consistency, relevance, and update status among the properties affecting fitness for use. A sound publication should therefore explain what the records cover, how they were prepared, and what remains uncertain. [s6]\n\nThe practical opportunity is to make decisions more inspectable: readers should be able to distinguish source records, analytical choices, and conclusions. This overview does not rank Iranian suppliers or estimate employment, revenue, or adoption. Those questions require dedicated evidence rather than an inference from the existence of software products.",
        "source_ids": ["s5", "s6"]
      }
    ],
